    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-350" contextRef="c-07">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 9.51pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 9.51pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 9.51pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 9.51pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 9.51pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-352" contextRef="c-07">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: unset; font-size: 1em; text-align: inherit"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Dixie Pipeline Company LLC (Dixie), is a Delaware limited liability company and a wholly owned subsidiary of Enterprise Products Operating LLC (EPOLLC), a Texas limited liability company, and is a consolidated subsidiary of Enterprise Products Partners L.P., a Delaware partnership, which is a publicly traded partnership.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Dixie is primarily a propane pipeline system that is approximately 1,300 miles in length. The system extends from southeast Texas and Louisiana to markets in the southeastern United States and the Texas gulf coast. Supplies transported on this system primarily originate from southeast Texas, southern Louisiana and Mississippi. The system operates in seven states: Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Alabama, Georgia, South Carolina and North Carolina. Dixie's property, plant and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Dixie is subject to regulation by various federal and state authorities, including the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC).&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting. The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Cash equivalents are defined as all highly marketable securities with maturities of three months or less when purchased. The carrying value of cash and cash equivalents approximates fair value because of the short term-to-maturity of these investments. Cash and cash equivalents includes FERC Account 11, Temporary Investments.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Dixie's revenues are primarily derived from transportation of propane under tariffs regulated by the FERC. The tariffs specify the amounts to be paid by shippers for service between receipt and delivery locations and the general terms and conditions of transportation services on the pipeline system. Revenues are recorded upon delivery of products to customers.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;During 2025, Dixie rebilled shippers for under-recovery resulting from the vacated January 20, 2022 rehearing order (Docket No. RM20-14-001) in the amount of $4,626,549.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; (See Commission's order issued on November 20, 2025 (Docket No. RM93-11-003, paragraph 37, footnote 111)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; These revenues are reported in account 645 &amp;quot;Unusual or Infrequent Items (credit)&amp;quot; on page 114.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Dixie is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the company to EPOLLC and, with the exception of the Texas Franchise Tax, if applicable, does not recognize this liability on the company's financial statements. For purposes of calculating income taxes for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report), Dixie employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Dixie has no employees of its own. All operations, management and administrative functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company on behalf of EPOLLC, the operator.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Dixie reimburses EPOLLC for management and administrative functions under the terms of an operating agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
